# TridentChain Security

When the user asks to scan dependencies, check supply-chain risk, or validate fixes after upgrades:

## Preferred: MCP (if configured)

If `tridentchain` MCP is enabled in `.cursor/mcp.json`, use:

- `scan_project` — fast project-only scan
- `scan_full` — project + system + IDE extensions
- `validate_after_patch` — compare baseline vs post-patch scan JSON

Install once:

```bash
pip3 install "tridentchain-security>=0.1.1" tridentchain-mcp
```

Copy [.cursor/mcp.json.example](../mcp.json.example) to `.cursor/mcp.json` and reload MCP.

## Fallback: CLI (always works)

```bash
tridentchain-security --scan all --project-path <workspace_root> --output-dir .tridentchain-out
```

Read `.tridentchain-out/scan-report.json` and HTML reports for details.

## Notes

- No API keys required for the default `full` profile.
- Use `--run-profile quick` for faster iteration.
- Do not paste secrets into chat; use environment variables for optional NVD/GitHub keys.

See [docs/CURSOR_SETUP.md](../../docs/CURSOR_SETUP.md) and [docs/AI_INTEGRATION.md](../../docs/AI_INTEGRATION.md).
